  "causal_summary": "Enacts Sophronia's inversion of permanence across two half-cities: the six western carnival structures (steep-humped roller coaster with suspended safety-bar shout, chain-spoked carousel, spinning-cage Ferris wheel, crouching-motorcyclist death-ride, trapeze big top, shooting galleries) are bolted into living bedrock and spark against every rigging wrench, whereas all ten eastern stone, marble, and cement institutions (bank, factories, palaces, slaughterhouse, school, Ministry, monument, docks, petroleum refinery, hospital) unbolt their marble pediments, stone walls, and cement pylons onto ten flatbed trailers, departing across the ochre square while the lone fairground counts the months and days until the caravan returns."
